    "chunk_text": "PRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 1\n\nPrice : Rs. 5.50Postage : Rs. 5.00\n\nPARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPublished as a Supplement to Part II of the Gazette of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka of March 31, 2006\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Certified on 27th March, 2006]\n\nPrinted on the Order of Government\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nCODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDURE(AMENDMENT)ACT, No. 7 OF 2006\n\nCode of Criminal Procedure (Amendment)Act, No. 7 of 20061\n\nShort title.\n\n[Certified on 27th March, 2006]\n\nL. D. \u2014 O. 64/2004\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE CODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDUREACT, NO. 15 OF1979\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows :-\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Code of CriminalProcedure (Amendment) Act, No. 7 of 2006.\n\n2.The First Schedule to the Code of Criminal ProcedureAct, No. 15 of 1979 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipalenactment\u201d) as last amended by Act, No. 28 of 1998 is herebyamended as follows:\u2014\n\n(1)by the insertion, immediately after the entry relatingto section 286A, of the following entries \u2014\n\nAmendment of theFirst Schedule toAct, No. 15 of1979.\n\n\u201c286B Failure ofpersonprovidingservicesbythe use ofcomputertopreventsexualabuseof child.\n\nSame SameSame Same Imprisonmentof eitherdescription fora term notexceeding twoyears or to afine or to bothsuchimprisonmentand fine.\n\nMagistrates\u2019Court\n\n286CFailure toinform ofuse ofpremisesfor childabuse.\n\nSame SameSame Same Imprisonmentof eitherdescriptionfor a term notexceedingtwo years orto a fine or toboth suchimprisonmentand fine.\u201d\n\nMagistrates\u2019Court\n\n2Code of Criminal Procedure (Amendment)Act, No. 7 of 2006\n\n\u201c358A DebtBondage,Serfdom,Forced orCompulsoryLabour, orSlavery.\n\nSameSameSameSameImprisonmentof eitherdescription fora term notexceedingtwenty yearsand fine."
